      'Two approaches to Indian kinship: Indological (Kapadia, Prabhu, Karve, Ghurye, from texts) and anthropological, split into descent (Gough, Madan, Mayer, Lewis) and alliance (Dumont) (IGNOU ESO-12 Unit 8).',
      'Karve (1953): four zones, northern, central, southern and eastern. Four dimensions to compare: kinship groups, terminology, marriage rules, gift exchange.',
